<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- What is bolted onto the stations: the second of the two documents the
     SiteNodeManager overlays onto its generated model.

     Every node here declares a parent that lives in Site.Layout.NodeSet2.xml
     (ns=1;i=5010 Station3), not in this file and not in the compiled model. That
     resolves because both documents are imported during ONE Configure pass, and the
     whole batch is linked exactly once after the pass returns. Import order does not
     matter; splitting the two files does not either.

     Reset carries a MethodDeclarationId of ns=1;i=13 - StationType/Reset in the
     compiled model - so the generated import factory materializes it as the model's
     ResetMethodState rather than as a plain MethodState. The InputArguments and
     OutputArguments Properties are spelled out here because an imported Method has
     exactly the children its document gives it: nothing is inherited from the
     declaration. -->
